{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1370,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Suppose we’re working with aliens who live\nnear Alpha Centauri to build a wormhole teleporter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5430,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we can go visit them - for dinner, or interstellar\ndiplomacy, or whatever. Of course we’ll"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9880,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "need to be able to talk with them about what\nto make each side of the portal out of, how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13110,
    "dDurationMs": 4950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "big to make the various pieces, and so on.\nBut since we’ve never been to Alpha Centauri,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18060,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they’ve never been here, this is tricky\n– I mean, if you tell me to make you an"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21720,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arc that’s 300 cubits long, and I don’t\nknow what a cubit is, you’ll probably get"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25770,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an arc that’s not exactly what you were\nhoping for ."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28510,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we’ll have to build, from the ground\nup, an easily sharable way of communicating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32770,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about the universe, where distances and such\nare based on ideas, rather than specific artifacts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37850,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ". We’d probably start with basic materials,\nyou know, like how instead of sending a vial"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41989,
    "dDurationMs": 4370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a chunk of lithium in it across interstellar\nspace, we can just say “use the atom that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46359,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has 3 protons, 3 neutrons, and 3 electrons.”\nWater would be “the molecule that’s a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51109,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "combination of one atom with 8 protons and\ntwo atoms with 1 proton.” And so on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56030,
    "dDurationMs": 4079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once we have materials down, we can do clocks\n– we just tell the aliens that if they take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60109,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the atom with 55 protons and 78 neutrons , make\nit emit a photon of light in a certain way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65030,
    "dDurationMs": 8010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ", and wait for that photon to oscillate 9,192,631,770\ntimes: that’s what we call one second."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73040,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once we have clocks, we can do distances:\njust tell the aliens to see how far light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76930,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes in one 299,792,458th of a second – that’s\nwhat we call a meter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82890,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this is when we would run into a massive\nroadblock – literally. Pretty much the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86910,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rest of our communication about the universe\nrequires knowing what mass is, and what we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91130,
    "dDurationMs": 4090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "currently call a kilogram isn’t an idea\nwe can just tell distant aliens, the way we"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95220,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can say “the atom with 3 protons”. A kilogram\nis just a particular lump of metal sitting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100080,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in a particular room in a particular place\non our planet , and if you want to know how"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103910,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many kilograms of say, antimatter, you have,\nyou have to take it there and weigh them against"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108730,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "each other .\nIn the very near future, we’re going to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110920,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "settle on a more sensible way of talking about\nmass, so instead of saying “in order to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114710,
    "dDurationMs": 3110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "build this teleporter you have to come to\nthe part of earth with good cheese so we can"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117820,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "show you our shiny lump of metal,” , we’ll\neither be telling the aliens to just get a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121160,
    "dDurationMs": 6969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pile of something like 21.5253873 septillion\nof the atom that has 14 protons and 14 neutrons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128129,
    "dDurationMs": 4521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or we’ll tell them to weigh how much mass\nan atom or molecule loses after emitting a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132650,
    "dDurationMs": 9590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "photon of light that oscillates roughly 135.6392534\nseptillion septillion times each second. One"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142240,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of these two concepts will be our new kilogram,\nand even though the pile of atoms option sounds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144640,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "simpler in principle, it’s actually kind\nof harder and more expensive to do in practice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145640,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Whichever way it is, once we have our new\nway of communicating about mass as an idea"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149090,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead of an object, we’ll be able to build\nour wormhole teleporter with the alpha centaurians"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153730,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": ". And then we can bring them here to earth,\nhave dinner, and afterwards, show them the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157920,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chunk of metal that used to be THE THING that\nwe used to talk about the mass of all other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163310,
    "dDurationMs": 4989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things.\nBefore I tell you about this video’s sponsor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168299,
    "dDurationMs": 4821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Skillshare, I want to tell you a story. I\nrecently turned 30, but back when I was in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173120,
    "dDurationMs": 4479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "high school, I was super into computer visual\neffects and sci-fi movies – however, there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 177599,
    "dDurationMs": 3581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were very few easy ways to learn how to do\nvisual effects yourself. I mean, consumer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181180,
    "dDurationMs": 4339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "access to digital video cameras was still\nvery new, personal computers were just starting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185519,
    "dDurationMs": 4011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be good enough for legit video editing,\nand youtube didn’t even exist. I had to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189530,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scrounge in vfx chat-rooms, dvd special features,\nand arcane blogs to learn enough to make my"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195010,
    "dDurationMs": 4539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lord-of-the-rings and star-wars parodies.\nToday at age 30, the situation is night and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199549,
    "dDurationMs": 4261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "day – you can shoot and edit high definition\nfootage on a telephone, for crying out loud!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203810,
    "dDurationMs": 3489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it’s much easier to learn how to use\nmore powerful tools like After Effects and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207299,
    "dDurationMs": 4761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Photoshop – services like Skillshare, for\nexample, now allow you to find tens of thousands"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212060,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of video tutorials on design, photography,\nprogramming, visual effects, and more. And"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216640,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Skillshare is offering 30% off a year-long\npremium membership for the first 200 people"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221090,
    "dDurationMs": 6289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who go to skl.sh/minutephysics30 – again,\nthat’s skl.sh/minutephysics30 for 30% off"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227379,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– and it works even if you didn’t just\nturn 30!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
